# sentence_id = 18
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = And just as they did not see fit to acknowledge God, God gave them over to a debased mind, to do the things that are not proper, filled with all unrighteousness, wickedness, greed, malice; full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, and depravity; whisperers, slanderers, haters of God, insolent, arrogant, boastful, inventors of evil things, disobedient to parents, senseless, faithless, without natural affection, unmerciful.
# literal_translation = And just as they did not approve to have God in [full] knowledge, God gave them over to a debased mind, to do the things not proper, having been filled with all unrighteousness, wickedness, greed, malice; full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, depravity; whisperers, slanderers, God-haters, insolent [ones], arrogant [ones], boasters, inventors of evils, disobedient to parents, senseless, faithless, unloving, unmerciful.
