# sentence_id = 100
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Therefore it is by faith, so that it may be according to grace, in order that the promise may be guaranteed to all the offspring—not only to the offspring who are of the law, but also to the offspring who are of the faith of Abraham (who is the father of us all, as it is written, 'I have made you a father of many nations'), before God, in whose presence he believed, the God who gives life to the dead and calls into being the things that do not exist as though they existed.
# literal_translation = Because of this, [it is] from faith, in order that [it may be] according to grace, for the promise to be sure to all the seed, not to that from the law only, but also to that from the faith of Abraham (who is father of all of us, just as it has been written, that, 'A father of many nations I have made you'), before whom he believed—of God, the one giving life to the dead and calling the things not existing as existing.
