# sentence_id = 447
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = so that from Jerusalem and round about as far as Illyricum I have fully proclaimed the gospel of Christ, making it my ambition in this way to preach the gospel not where Christ had already been named, so that I might not build on another man's foundation, but, as it is written, 'They who had no report of him shall see, and they who have not heard shall understand.'
# literal_translation = So-that I, from Jerusalem and in-a-circle as-far-as Illyricum, [am] having-fulfilled the gospel of-the Christ, but thus making-it-my-ambition to-preach-the-gospel not where Christ was-named, in-order-that not upon another's foundation I-might-build, but as it-has-been-written, 'They-shall-see, to-whom it-was-not-announced concerning him, and they who have-not-heard shall-understand.'
